"use strict";

/* generated from story/scenes/act3_ch13.md — do not edit */

SC["a3c13_open"]={t:()=>SYS(`ACT THREE — THE RIVERS AND LAKES`)+SYS(`CHAPTER THIRTEEN — DOWN THE THOUSAND STEPS`)+P(`Morning at the top of the steps, and the mountain is waiting for its answer.`)+P(`The elders' offer sits on one side of you like a folded robe: inner court, a courtyard, archive rights, a seat at the foot of the table. On the other side sits a margin note in a dead man's ledger and a riverhouse address two weeks downriver, where a silkworm seal has been collecting a season-tithe of harvested soul-heat for forty years — and will collect another one this season, and the next, from mountains that have their own kitchens, their own Meis, their own holes in the garden books.`)+P(`You watched the lanterns climb last night until the cold ran out of arguments. There was never really a version of this where you didn't already know.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Take the writ. Leave with the sect's blessing, its stipend, and its expectations stitched into your sleeve.`,do:()=>{G.f.a3_route="sect";},go:"a3c13_sect"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Take the road. Leave tonight, by the firewood paths, owing nothing and owed nothing.`,do:()=>{G.f.a3_route="road";},go:"a3c13_road"}]};

SC["a3c13_sect"]={t:()=>P(`The elders, to their credit, do not pretend to be surprised. What follows is three days of the institution doing what institutions do best: converting an inconvenient hero into paperwork.`)+P(`The writ they draft is, you suspect, somebody's idea of a joke with forty years of teeth in it: <i>itinerant auditor, empowered to examine the accounts of allied and tributary halls</i> — Steward Qiu's old title, dusted off and hung on the one person on the mountain who made auditing dangerous. A stipend. A jade tally for the post-stations. A list of halls that owe the Azure Cloud courtesy, and a thinner, unwritten list of what the sect would prefer not to learn about itself while you're out there.`)+P(`Yan Shuo walks you to the head of the steps. “The record stays open here,” he says, eyes on the valley. “Whatever you find downriver, send it to me unvarnished. I'll decide what the elders can stomach.” A pause, one degree of warmth: “The frozen stream is better in summer. Come back and see it.”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The steps go down. For the first time in two years, so do you.`,go:"a3c13_steps"}]};

SC["a3c13_road"]={t:()=>P(`You leave the way you arrived: with nothing official.`)+P(`Auntie Tang packs you a travel bundle with the ruthless economy of a woman who has packed for every kind of leaving — twice-baked cakes, a sewing kit, the pot-iron charm checked and re-knotted on its cord. She doesn't say goodbye. She says “eat the soft ones first,” which in Tang is the same sentence with the grief folded in.`)+P(`Bao gives you a sleeve. Literally — he sewed it himself, badly, which is how you know he didn't delegate: a row of chandler's addresses stitched in knot-code down the inner seam, one for every river town from here to the lake country. “Firewood boys know everything,” he says, “and chandlers know the firewood boys. Anywhere there's a candle, you can get a message to me.” He grips your shoulder hard enough to bruise and leaves before either of you can do anything worse — his signature move, twice now.`)+P(`Nobody official watches you go. You feel the difference all the way down: missed by exactly the people who matter, and by no one else.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The steps go down. For the first time in two years, so do you.`,go:"a3c13_steps"}]};

SC["a3c13_steps"]={img:"steps",
 t:()=>P(`A thousand steps, walked the wrong way.`)+P(`You came up them half-drowned in the dark on another soul's last legs, and so this is, in every way that counts, the first time you have ever seen them: the stair falling away through cloud terraces like a seam down the world's coat, pine and granite giving way to bamboo, bamboo to tea slopes, the dragon vein's silver note thinning underfoot step by step until somewhere around the eight-hundredth stair it slips below hearing, and the mountain — the whole humming, knotted, load-bearing mountain — becomes, simply, sky behind you.`)+((G.f.a1_intent=="home")?(P(`Every step down is a step away from the only door you know of, and you take them anyway, because you've learned which direction promises actually travel: the road home doesn't run up the mountain. It runs through the people who keep furnaces, and the Court that franchises them, and whatever sits at the Grand Loom holding the deeds. You'll come back up these steps someday. You intend to come back up them holding the key.`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent=="strong")?(P(`The realm-doors don't live on the mountain — that was the mountain's best-kept lie. Loomheart opened in a furnace hall, not a meditation cell. Whatever Pattern Sage costs, it's down here somewhere, in the wide world's worth of weave the sect never taught because the sect never knew. You go down the steps the way other men climb.`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent=="even")?(P(`Somewhere below, a kind river sect is beloved by its servants and paid for by a furnace. The books don't balance just because nobody local can read them. You are, by writ or by nature, an auditor now — and the audit the basement taught you doesn't stop at one mountain's ledgers.`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent=="safe")?(P(`Staying was the unsafe choice — that's the arithmetic nobody up there would say out loud. The Court has your name on forty years of receipts; behind sect walls you're a fixed address with a famous head of hair. On the river you're a rumor. Rumors are hard to harvest.`)):(""))+P(`By the time the steps run out, the sun is down the sky and the river smell comes up to meet you — mud and rope and fish and woodsmoke, the smell of a world that doesn't know your name yet.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The first town at the mountain's foot.`,go:"a3c13_town"}]};

SC["a3c13_town"]={t:()=>P(`Cloudrest-Below-the-Steps is everything the mountain isn't: loud, low, wet, and gloriously indifferent. Porters argue. Geese audit the market with more authority than you've ever managed. A wine-shop's lantern promises exactly what it can deliver. Nobody bows. One small child points at your hair and is hauled off by the ear before completing the observation, and you stand in the middle of the street grinning like a fool at the sheer unwoven ordinariness of it.`)+P(`The riverhouse coordinates from Kang's receipts sit two weeks downriver, in the lake country where the merchants' water-roads all knot together. Passage is easy to buy and cheap.`)+((G.f.a2_mei_bench=="robbed"&&G.mei>=3)?(P(`And at the chandler's — Bao's first address — a familiar crate is waiting on the loading boards, stamped with a herb-mark you'd know anywhere: Mei's salve, jar by jar, working its way down the same river. The chandler, once convinced you're you, hands over a letter in dosage-instruction script: <i>The trade runs the river towns through the lake country. If a gold-haired idiot happens downriver, the trade can find him. Try not to need stitches before Third Reed Town. — M.</i>`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Buy passage downriver. The receipts have an address; go introduce yourself.`,do:()=>{G.f.a3_mei_present=(G.f.a2_mei_bench=="robbed"&&G.mei>=3);G.f.a3_loud=0;},go:"a3c14_bridge"}]};